  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A fine-sand cove split in two by a rocky point, with the Îles d'Or in the background. Canadel beach keeps a wild feel and stays on a human scale, away from the bustle of nearby Saint-Tropez — a genuinely good option for a quiet walk with your dog outside swimming hours.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>From 1 June to 30 September, dogs are not admitted on the beach between 8am and 7pm. Outside this summer period, or early in the morning / in the evening in summer, your dog can enjoy the sand and water with you.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: come in spring or autumn instead to have the beach almost to yourself — that's when Canadel is most pleasant with a dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Domaine du Rayol, a remarkable botanical garden nearby, does not allow dogs, even on leash — worth knowing if you're planning to stop there along the way.</p>
